For third person (singular and plural) possessed nouns, that end in a vowel, when it comes to taking case suffixes, a letter {{lang|ota|ـنـ}} ({{translit|ota|-n-}}) comes after the possessive suffix. For singular endings, the final vowel {{lang|ota|ـی}} ({{translit|ota|-ı}} or {{translit|ota|-i}}) is removed in all instances. For plural endings, if the letter succeeding the additional {{lang|ota|ـنـ}} ({{translit|ota|-n-}}) is a vowel, the final vowel {{lang|ota|ـی}} ({{translit|ota|-ı}} or {{translit|ota|-i}}) is kept; otherwise it is removed (note the respective examples for {{lang|ota-Latn|kitaplarını}} and {{lang|ota-Latn|kitaplarından}}).

